# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and most of its files are stored with
# CRLF, which is left alone deliberately: renormalising them would rewrite every
# file for no benefit and bury real changes under whole-file diffs.
#
# The exception is anything that has to RUN on the Linux VPS. A shell script
# committed with CRLF fails with `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or
# directory` -- a message that reads like a missing interpreter and sends you
# looking for the wrong problem entirely. It cost a debugging detour once; this
# file is so it cannot cost another.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Certificates and keys are bytes, not text.
*.pem           binary
*.crx           binary
